  "notes": "Can mean both the act of collecting donations and the donated money itself. In everyday life, {募金|ぼきん} is often seen at train stations, convenience stores, and disaster relief campaigns.\n\nNote the usage difference: {募金|ぼきん}する can mean either to donate or to raise funds depending on context, though in common usage it more often means to donate.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {募金|ぼきん}する — to donate; to raise funds\n- {募金|ぼきん}{活動|かつどう} — fundraising activity\n- {募金|ぼきん}{箱|ばこ} — donation box\n- {街頭|がいとう}{募金|ぼきん} — street-corner fundraising\n- {赤|あか}い{羽根|はね}{募金|ぼきん} — Red Feather Community Chest",
